ll (24,645 cumulative chips won until last hand), preserving equity matters, but maximizing expected value is still key.\n\nBest play: **Raise for value**. Many players will call with weaker flushes (e.g., 7♥x, 5♥x, etc.). Even one pair hands might call thinking you\'re bluffing.\n\nMinimum raise is 278. Since you have 19,800, going all-in is overkill (~20k), unlikely to be called unless they have the nuts.\n\nOptimal: **Raise to 278 or slightly more** to extract value without scaring away worse hands.\n\nBut note: raising 278 means you’re putting in an additional 278 (total bet of 278, whereas the opponent’s bet was 139). That’s a proper raise.\n\nAlternatively, larger raise risks folding out worse hands.\n\nThus, best action: **raise by 278**, minimum raise, for value.\n\nReason: You have a strong flush, likely the best hand. Raising extracts value from weaker flushes and some one-pair hands that misjudge the situation. Folding loses value. Checking (calling) leaves money on the table.\n\nAnswer: 278'}
