ked back turn and river, indicating weakness. A small raise can represent a strong hand (like a flush or top two pair) and induce a fold from hands like A-K, Q-10, or missed draws. The cost is low (100 chips), and you are ahead in chips overall, so preserving stack isn't critical, but maximizing fold equity with minimal risk is optimal.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
